- `opt.rs` has two sealed array traits since options wave 1: `ArrayElement` (batch 0, owned outputs of `get_array`: `Option<HeapString>`, `Dict`, `ChannelLayoutVal`) and `ArrayInput` (batch 1, borrowed inputs of `insert_array`/`replace_array`: `&CStr`, `Option<&CStr>`, `ChannelLayoutRef`, `Option<DictionaryRef>`, plus the plain types). `tests/common/opt.rs` has two array fixtures: batch 0's `ArrObj`/`ArrOwned` (defaults for every type) and batch 1's `Arrays`/`OwnedArrays` (child, size bounds, wide rationals, read-only, scalar; `zeroed_with_child()` skips C's default parses, which BSan misreports at `eval.c:120`, so BSan-targeted tests use it).
