13:- Keep `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` outside the worktree (e.g. `/tmp/<batch>/{asan,tsan,bsan,miri}`): an untracked `target/` inside it is easy to wipe or commit.
26:- ASan/UBSan, TSan: `CRUSTIFY_FFMPEG_VARIANT=<asan-ubsan|tsan> RUSTFLAGS=-Zsanitizer=<address|thread> CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<outside>/<unique> cargo +nightly test -Zbuild-std --target x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu --lib --tests -- --skip compile_fail`. Skip `compile_fail`: under `-Zbuild-std` rustc adds `$RUST/core` source notes, so trybuild `.stderr` blessed on stable mismatches. Whole-crate ASan and TSan passes take ~5 min each with a fresh target dir.
35:- OOM branches the `av_max_alloc` limit never reaches (e.g. `av_fast_realloc`, `fast_malloc`): an isolated-child test spawned through `sh -c 'ulimit -v 524288 && exec "$0" "$@"' <exe> --exact <name>` asking for 1 GiB fails them deterministically on plain and coverage builds. Skip it under asan-ubsan/tsan/bsan, whose runtimes cannot start under such a limit.
